.TH "SOPLOS-LAYOUT-SWITCHER" "1" "2026-11-17" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-layout-switcher \- GNOME Shell layout presets for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-layout-switcher
.br
.B soplos-layout-switcher-cli
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-layout-switcher
switches the GNOME Shell desktop between four predefined layouts, Soplos, Dock,
Tiling and GNOME, by turning on the shell extensions each one needs, turning
off those of the other layouts and applying the matching settings. Built with
Tauri 2, Rust and Svelte, it only runs under GNOME Shell, with X11 or Wayland.
.P
Its window shows the four layouts with a picture each, and has the buttons to
apply the chosen one and to reload the desktop. A gear at the bottom right of
the banner opens the settings as a sidebar at the left of the layouts, which
makes the window wider and gives that room back when it is closed. The
settings have a switch for the system tray and one for the desktop icons, and
buttons that open
GNOME Tweaks, Refine (an alternative to it), the extensions manager, GNOME
Settings (for the accent color), GDM Settings and Add Water, which themes
Firefox. Refine and Add Water are Flatpaks, installed for the user the first
time.
.P
The button Save current layout keeps the desktop as it is, with a name: the
extensions that are on, their settings and the window buttons. The layouts
saved are shown after the four, can be applied and deleted, and are also
accepted by the command line.
.P
Before a layout is applied, the extensions it needs are installed if they are
missing: from their Debian package, which is installed as administrator with
.BR pkexec (1)
and asks for the password once; from the extensions that ship with the program
(Forge and Open Bar, which have no package); or from extensions.gnome.org.
Whatever cannot be installed is left to the user in the extensions manager.
.P
Five extensions are taken as the user's own taste and are never touched:
Coverflow Alt-Tab, Clipboard Indicator, Desktop Cube, Removable Drive Menu and
User Themes.
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English.
.SH COMMAND LINE
.B soplos-layout-switcher-cli
does the same without a window, for scripts and installers:
.TP
.B apply-soplos, apply-dock, apply-gnome, apply-tiling
Apply the layout.
.TP
.B reload-gnome-shell
Reload the desktop: restart the shell on X11, close the session on Wayland.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Escape
Close the settings sidebar.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/soplos-layout-switcher.conf
Keeps the layout applied last, under [SETTING].
.TP
.I ~/.config/soplos-layout-switcher/layouts/
The layouts saved by the user, one JSON file each.
.TP
.I /usr/share/soplos-layout-switcher/extensions/
Extensions that ship with the program.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/gnome-shell/extensions/
Where the extensions are installed for the user.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.soplos.layoutswitcher.policy
Polkit policy for the installation of the packages of the extensions.
